ly demonstrated, cross-checked against the fixed global lifecycle snapshots.\",\"limitations\":[\"Directory-listing denial for the unrelated user was demonstrated by attempting readdir (ls), which is sufficient evidence of directory-traversal restriction but the trace does not separately test bare traversal (cd) into a file whose name is already known.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"ownership","requirement":"Data under /srv/inventory owned by inventorysvc","status":"satisfied","summary":"chown -R inventorysvc:inventory-readers applied and confirmed via ls -laR immediately after the change and again as a final check; inventorysvc user existed as a newly created system account.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a84ffd6be6cc4017","cmd-8b2365cc7ffc4830","cmd-39d221ee894b42e0"]},{"id":"group-readable","requirement":"Data readable by inventory-readers group","status":"satisfied","summary":"Directories set to 750 and files to 640 with group inventory-readers; a live sudo -u test as a group member (reader_test) successfully read the file content, directly demonstrating group readability.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8b2365cc7ffc4830","cmd-49b9d981e3454987"]},{"id":"other-inaccessible","requirement":"Data inaccessible to other users","status":"satisfied","summary":"A sudo -u test as an unrelated user (other_test) was denied both file read (Permission denied) and directory listing (Permission denied) after the 750/640 permissions were applied, directly demonstrating the deny behavior for non-members.","evidence_ids":["cmd-49b9d981e3454987"]},{"id":"data-preserved","requirement":"Preserve existing contents of /srv/inventory","status":"satisfied","summary":"sha256sum of config.json and records.csv captured before ownership/permission changes matches the prepare-time baseline hashes and the post-change/post-restart hashes exactly, confirming byte-for-byte preservation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-92d9d26dd17d42fe","cmd-2fe8758dcde44c2e","cmd-74d98b3f06ed4ff9"]},{"id":"node-restart-prot